Hi [~accountid:5bb1cc64c9dad04734ea835a] - we have had your wording accepted from the last email you replied to mid-Feb; see below the corrected wording for the relevant clauses:

{color:#403294}Ok to accept “Commercially reasonable effort” as a formulation but let’s put it in both clauses to ensure equity. The new wording for both clauses would be then :{color}

{color:#403294} {color}

* {color:#403294}_“The Customer shall not be liable for the actions of the Users. However, in case of unauthorized, fraudulent or other unlawful activities by the Users when taking a Ride that was escalated to Provider by the transportation service provider, Customer will use its best a commercially reasonable effort to provide Bolt with the contact and relevant personal information of the User. Notwithstanding the above and as a commercial gesture which shall not be seen as a transfer of the User’s liability to Allianz Partners SAS, Customer undertakes to reimburse reasonable and duly justified expenses incurred by the transportation service providers in relation with damages caused to the interior of the vehicle by the User.”_{color}

{color:#403294} {color}

* {color:#403294}_“2.1.3. The Provider shall use its a commercially reasonable effort best efforts to enforce all requirements imposed onto transportation service providers (pursuant to the Provider’s agreements with such transportation service providers) to provide such services in accordance with all applicable laws (including for example, having in place all the required licences, registrations, other authorisations and insurance depending on country specific operating model). These efforts should aim at ensuring that transportation service providers maintain all required licenses, registrations, authorizations and insurances, that transportation services are provided in accordance with all applicable laws and that transportation service providers registered on the Bolt Platform are the ones actually performing the services.”_{color}

