Hey Peerasorn, 

In order to attach a fee calculator to a company, we would need the following information:

* *Commission rate*: Commission percentage that will apply per ride to the driver/fleet. {color:#ff5630}(Once attached, can only be changed on the next day){color}
* *Currency*: Usually country default if not stated otherwise
* [*Invoicing strategy*|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/1603895624/Fee+calculators+and+invoicing+strategies#Invoicing-strategy]: Driver or Company. This will define to whom payouts will go, and invoices will be issued. {color:#ff5630}(Once attached, can only be changed on the first day of next month){color}
* *Booking fee:* Is there an active booking fee in the city? If so, do you want it to be deducted from the driver (and reflected on the commission invoice), or be a 100% driver income? {color:#ff5630}(Can be updated anytime){color}
* *Cash-blocking thresholds*: Defines the cash ride limits for blocking/unblocking cash rides for a driver. This can be copied from other cities, but please discuss with [{color:#b3f5ff}Billing Analytics{color}|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/1240/create/806] if your market is cash-heavy. {color:#ff5630}(Can be updated anytime){color}
** Max negative balance before messaging: The threshold where we will notify the driver that they are getting closer to being cash-blocked
** Max negative balance before removing cash payments: The debt threshold we allow cash rides up to. After the driver exceeds this threshold, cash orders will be disabled.
** Minimal balance to unblock cash rides: The balance threshold where we will once again unblock the driver’s cash rides.

